      "text" : "Summary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "dac238b5",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Adds a new Supplier root bean (name, contactEmail with email validation, country, active) from the spec's descriptor and default form, exposes it through an observer sheet, and builds the Suppliers screen from its mock: a name-sorted table with inactive rows greyed out but kept, and a side panel with the default form. It is registered under Procurement › Suppliers, in three tasks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "feature-design-h",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 2
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Design"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "c0835ff2",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Supplier entity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "8aeedb35",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Grounding: the spec's Dependencies are \"None\"; Supplier is a genuinely new root bean in package "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "procurement",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ", so nothing is reused or re-modelled. Fields follow the spec's Data model: "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "name",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (text, required), "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "contactEmail",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (text, optional, email-address format validation on save), "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "country",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (text, optional), "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "active",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (flag, required). There are no references, enums or embedded beans. Nothing is migrated (new table only)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "4f5fc132",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "The entity descriptor "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "entity_descriptors/procurement.Supplier.json",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " and the default form "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "ui/procurement.Supplier.js",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " are authored at spec time and copied verbatim into the module. The entity class is built from the descriptor. The observer sheet is the entity's only remote surface, and the screen reads and writes through it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "8b4773a3",
